WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.760
Scrape your knee. In about one to two weeks, new skin often covers the spot.

2
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.820
Where did those new skin cells come from?

3
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.400
Every cell comes from a cell that was already there.

4
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.520
One cell splits and becomes two.

5
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.580
Most cells carry a full set of instructions.

6
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.020
How does each new cell get a complete set?

7
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:32.113
A cell that divides goes through the cell cycle.

8
00:00:32.713 --> 00:00:36.653
It is the series of steps from when a cell forms until it divides.

9
00:00:37.373 --> 00:00:38.993
It has two main parts.

10
00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:43.293
Interphase is when the cell grows and copies its chromosomes.

11
00:00:44.293 --> 00:00:47.913
Chromosomes are the threads in the nucleus that carry the cell's instructions.

12
00:00:48.893 --> 00:00:51.813
During interphase the cell is busy, not resting.

13
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:56.333
Mitosis is when the cell divides into two new cells.

14
00:00:57.183 --> 00:01:00.423
Picture a model cell with four chromosomes.

15
00:01:01.223 --> 00:01:04.003
In interphase, each chromosome is copied.

16
00:01:04.603 --> 00:01:07.363
A copied chromosome is still one chromosome.

17
00:01:07.903 --> 00:01:11.103
It is made of two identical copies joined together.

18
00:01:11.763 --> 00:01:14.183
So the cell still has four chromosomes.

19
00:01:14.803 --> 00:01:16.943
Each one now has two copies.

20
00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:19.917
Now mitosis begins.

21
00:01:20.657 --> 00:01:24.657
It has four stages, and they always come in the same order.

22
00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:29.797
In prophase, the chromosomes coil up and get thick enough to see.

23
00:01:30.677 --> 00:01:35.557
In metaphase, the chromosomes line up in a row across the middle of the cell.

24
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:42.120
In anaphase, the two copies of each chromosome are pulled to opposite ends.

25
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.240
Thin fibers in the cell do the pulling.

26
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.400
In telophase, two new nuclei form, and the cell pinches into two.

27
00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.860
Each new cell is called a daughter cell.

28
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.900
The cell that divided is the parent cell.

29
00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:01.973
So how does each daughter cell get a complete set?

30
00:02:03.073 --> 00:02:04.233
Copying comes first.

31
00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:08.533
Then one copy of each chromosome goes to each new cell.

32
00:02:09.473 --> 00:02:13.773
Each daughter cell ends up with four chromosomes, the same as the parent cell.

33
00:02:14.813 --> 00:02:17.993
Skip the copying, and each daughter cell would get only two.

34
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:23.713
Copy first, then share, and the instructions are not mixed up or lost.
